    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Dobbm',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Dobbm is a traditional trick-taking game unique to the Stubai Valley in Tyrol, Austria. It is an 'Ace-Ten' game related to Tarock and Tapp, played with a 36-card Tell-pattern deck. The name refers to the 4-card talon known as the 'Dobb'.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Dobbm is a hyper-local tradition centered in the village of Fulpmes. It was documented in 1996 by John McLeod and Remigius Geiser.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "4 active players. If 5 play, the dealer 'feiert' (takes a holiday) and sits out.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36 German-suited (Tell) cards. Suits: Hearts, Leaves, Acorns, Bells.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '36-card deck, score sheet.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "8 cards to each player dealt in batches of 4. Four cards go face-down to the center as the 'Dobb'. The dealer for a hand is always the 'declarer' from the previous hand.",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
