          equipment: '36-card deck, score sheet.',
          dealing: "8 cards to each player dealt in batches of 4. Four cards go face-down to the center as the 'Dobb'. The dealer for a hand is always the 'declarer' from the previous hand.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win tricks to capture point cards and reach a target score. Points are: Ace/Sow (11), Ten (10), King (4), Ober (3), Unter (2). Total: 120 points per hand.',
          gameplay: "1. Bidding: Players bid 'Ordinary' or 'Solo'. In an Ordinary game, the declarer takes the 'Dobb' and discards 4 cards (points count for them).\n2. Trumps: Declarer names the trump suit.\n3. The Dobb: In a Solo, the Dobb points count for the dealer (who is celebrating), not the soloist.\n4. Card Play: Clockwise. Must follow suit. If unable, must play a trump if possible.",
          keyRules: [
            "The 6 of Bells ('Weli') is just a normal card in Dobbm.",
            "The Ace is called the 'Sow' (Sau).",
            "Defenders can 'schieben' (smear) points on their partner's trick.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "As declarer, discard weak suits into the Dobb to create 'voids' for trumping.",
          intermediate: "Use 'schinden' - defenders holding back high cards to win later tricks with established winners.",
          advanced: "Recognize a 'Fuchs' (fox) - a single card in a suit that can be played to trick opponents into believing you have more of that suit.",
          tips: [
            'The Heart Sow is the most powerful trump starter.',
            "Don't lead your top trumps immediately; force defenders to use theirs on side-suit tricks.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
