          customActions: [],
          deckDescription: 'One 36-card German-suited deck used for Dobbm in the Stubai Valley: four suits (Acorns, Leaves, Hearts, Bells) with nine ranks per suit (6, 7, 8, 9, 10, Unter, Ober, King, Ace). No jokers; the deck is the standard stripped German pack for point-trick games in Tyrol.',
          suitDescription: 'Four German suits: Acorns (Eichel), Leaves (Laub), Hearts (Herz), Bells (Schellen), each with nine cards. In Dobbm, trump is chosen by the bid winner; follow suit and overtrump when able, and eight tricks are played per deal.',
          rankDescription: 'Nine ranks per suit from low to high: 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, Unter, Ober, King, Ace. Point values follow Ace-Ten scoring (e.g. Ace 11, Ten 10, King 4, Ober 3, Unter 2, numeral 0) as used in Dobbm and regional Tyrolean games.',
          dealPattern: 'Deal 8 each and set 4-card Dobb talon.',
